            <ArticleTitle>Chronic Hypersensitivity Pneumonia due to Pigeon Breeders Disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>55-57</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Pigeon breeders disease usually affects adults. Children are more likely to be affected when they share living space with a backyard poultry or pigeon breeding.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE CHARACTERISTICS" NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED">A 12-year-old girl with persistent cough for 3 years and dyspnea for 2 years.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OBERVATION" NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED">She was dignosed to be having allergy to pigeon droppings, based on reports of lung biopsy and allergy testing.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MESSAGE" NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED">Pigeon breaders disease should be considered in a child who presents with features of chronic hypersensiticity pneumonitis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
